  "query_preview": "../ Thursday to Monday / Aloft the steering levels of \nthe atmosphere has a long wave trough finally being ejected from \nthe gulf late Thursday to Friday, followed by a sharper moderate-\nhigh amplitude ridge that reaches near to arctic shores. Ridge \nwill slide east of the panhandle by late Sunday, as the Large \nBering Sea low from the western Bering Sea weakens but shift to \nthe eastern portion of the Bering. With the ridge axis east of the\narea, noticed a pair of short waves, one Sunday evening pushing \nthrough the panhandle over the ridge top, and second one which may\nbe slightly stronger for the Monday time frame. So what does this\nmean weather wise for Southeast... showers from the midweek into \nThursday, tapering off/ending as improvements Friday - early \nSaturday period due to the ridge moving through and clearing \nweather out. After the ridge slides by rain will start to push \nback in into the NE Gulf then Northern panhandle late Saturday to \nSunday. Models beginning to come to agreement of fairly organized \nfrom to push through the eastern gulf Sunday to Monday. A \nsecondary low that formed on the front towards the Yakutat Pocket \nand the front trailing south then southwest, with likely another \ntrailing low on the front to run along and slowing it down to \nimpact the southern panhandle most likely the hardest. Will watch \nhow models adjust over the next few runs. In short longer range is\nwet, dry break Friday-Saturday and then wet into next week. \nTemperature-wise at or just below normal values, with higher \nelevations of the Klondike and the higher Canadian Haines Highways\nto possible see snow or snow rain mix for the weekend period.",
